I'd been chronicling this game a bit in the "Ink shortage and pet
advice" thread. So now I see why many extinctionist posts have said
"never again"... after a month of playing on and off, I just didn't
have the patience anymore. I only managed to extinct 19 species. But I
did achieve certain goals:

- First score over 10 million points
- Learned every spell, and all at 0% failure
- HP and power over 1000 (HP is trivially easy to increase with
alchemy though)
- AC below -50 (despite losing 13 points of protection in an early
prayer accident)
- Ascended with pet (flying on my ki-rin)

And other more trivial things:
- Made a bunch of +8 elven daggers (though didn't end up using them)
- Got one piece of armor enchanted to +7 (small shield)
- Got over 100 dilithium, plus many other gems but couldn't carry
everything

More amusements:
-  I had two Archons for much of the late game, and managed to get one
all the way to Astral.  Then I got confused by an umber hulk and
accidentally decapitated poor Archie just before getting to the right
altar. He had an AoLS but was in no mood to talk to me when he came
back to life.
- After easily avoiding mind flayers for nearly the entire (genoless)
game I got flayed twice on Astral. I wasn't using conflict (until my
Archon died) and was Burdened, which certainly contributed.
Fortunately I didn't forget anything important.

